From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:19:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [tests] Drop the analysis findings the last fixes took away.

cppcheck no longer finds the two conditions in the ofono provider and
its factory that the modem list handling replaced, nor gcc's analyzer the
uninitialised value in the D-Bus service's call removal.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tests/hardening/static-analysis.baseline | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/hardening/static-analysis.baseline b/tests/hardening/static-analysis.baseline
index 157aaae..1be0a94 100644
--- a/tests/hardening/static-analysis.baseline
+++ b/tests/hardening/static-analysis.baseline
@@ -52,9 +52,7 @@ clang-tidy: src/dbus/voicecallhandlerdbusadapter.cpp: returning a constant refer
   why: QDBusArgument operator>> must return the const QDBusArgument & it was given; Qt's D-Bus marshalling signature
 cppcheck: plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallhandler.h: Virtual function 'status' is called from constructor 'OfonoVoiceCallHandler(const QString&handlerId,const QString&path,OfonoVoiceCallProvider*provider,QOfonoVoiceCallManager*manager)' at line 74. Dynamic binding is not used. [virtualCallInConstructor]
   why: the handler classes are not subclassed; the call is meant to reach this class's own implementation
-cppcheck: plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallprovider.cpp: Condition '!d->ofonoManager->isValid()' is always false [knownConditionTrueFalse]
   why: false positive: QOfonoManager::isValid() is only declared in the header, cppcheck guesses its value
-cppcheck: plugins/providers/ofono/src/ofonovoicecallproviderfactory.cpp: Pointer expression 'this' converted to bool is always true. [knownPointerToBool]
   why: false positive: 'new QOfonoManager(this)' passes the parent, nothing is converted to bool
 cppcheck: plugins/providers/telepathy/src/callchannelhandler.h: Virtual function 'lineId' is called from constructor 'CallChannelHandler(const QString&id,Tp::CallChannelPtr channel,const QDateTime&userActionTime,TelepathyProvider*provider=0)' at line 103. Dynamic binding is not used. [virtualCallInConstructor]
   why: the handler classes are not subclassed; the call is meant to reach this class's own implementation
@@ -124,7 +122,6 @@ fanalyzer: src/dbus/voicecallhandlerdbusadapter.cpp: use of uninitialized value
   why: false positive of GCC 15's experimental C++ analyzer on Qt implicitly shared temporaries (QString from a literal, QList/QHash copies); the reported paths end in Qt's reference counting
 fanalyzer: src/dbus/voicecallmanagerdbusadapter.cpp: use of uninitialized value '<unknown>' [CWE-457] [-Wanalyzer-use-of-uninitialized-value]
   why: false positive of GCC 15's experimental C++ analyzer on Qt implicitly shared temporaries (QString from a literal, QList/QHash copies); the reported paths end in Qt's reference counting
-fanalyzer: src/dbus/voicecallmanagerdbusservice.cpp: use of uninitialized value '<unknown>' [CWE-457] [-Wanalyzer-use-of-uninitialized-value]
   why: false positive of GCC 15's experimental C++ analyzer on Qt implicitly shared temporaries (QString from a literal, QList/QHash copies); the reported paths end in Qt's reference counting
 flawfinder: plugins/declarative/src/voicecallaudiorecorder.cpp: [2] (misc) open
   why: QFile/QSqlDatabase::open(), not open(2): the files are the catalog (root-owned), the database and recordings in the user's own private directory, with sanitised names
